WEBVTT

00:00:00.840 --> 00:00:02.690
Good morning!

00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:08.360
Yaguchi Kyouya?

00:00:08.780 --> 00:00:11.150
I've seen that name somewhere.

00:00:12.980 --> 00:00:16.600
Are you the new girl?

00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:20.080
Yes, hello. I'm...

00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:23.860
Miyuki-chan?

00:00:24.770 --> 00:00:26.130
You're Miyuki-chan, right?

00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:27.260
N-No...

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:28.810
What are you doing here?

00:00:28.810 --> 00:00:30.990
I was hoping I'd see you again.

00:00:30.990 --> 00:00:33.370
Um... You've got the wrong person.

00:00:33.370 --> 00:00:35.010
No, I don't.

00:00:35.390 --> 00:00:38.510
I never forget a girl I've slept with.

00:02:13.110 --> 00:02:17.280
"Starry Sky"

00:02:13.580 --> 00:02:17.400
Huh? But your name wasn't on the schedule.

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:19.490
I told you. I'm...

00:02:19.880 --> 00:02:23.470
Yaguchi, get your ass out here already.

00:02:23.470 --> 00:02:26.430
Asami-chan, I know this girl.

00:02:26.430 --> 00:02:28.060
What are you talking about?

00:02:28.060 --> 00:02:30.840
Her name's Miyuki-chan. 
She's stayed at my place.

00:02:30.840 --> 00:02:32.170
Um...!

00:02:33.510 --> 00:02:35.430
You have the wrong person.

00:02:35.430 --> 00:02:37.800
My name is Ogiwara Sayu.

00:02:38.600 --> 00:02:40.760
But you said your name was "Miyuki-chan"—

00:02:41.810 --> 00:02:43.790
This is Sayu-chaso.

00:02:43.790 --> 00:02:45.130
Are you an idiot?

00:02:45.130 --> 00:02:47.020
And get back out there.

00:02:47.020 --> 00:02:48.990
Come on. I'm just on a short break.

00:02:48.990 --> 00:02:50.670
There's nothing going on here.

00:02:51.230 --> 00:02:53.800
Shut up and get out there!

00:02:56.820 --> 00:02:57.990
Asami...

00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:01.370
Um... I...

00:03:01.370 --> 00:03:02.340
It's fine.

00:03:03.110 --> 00:03:04.220
It's fine.

00:03:04.220 --> 00:03:06.040
You don't need to tell me.

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:06.660
But...

00:03:07.680 --> 00:03:11.220
Sayu-chaso, you don't seem like 
you want to talk about it.

00:03:12.520 --> 00:03:16.960
If you don't want to tell someone, 
you don't have to tell them, okay?

00:03:18.590 --> 00:03:24.010
But if you ever feel like telling me, you can!

00:03:29.140 --> 00:03:32.660
<i>Yaguchi-san hasn't talked to me since.</i>

00:03:34.930 --> 00:03:37.200
Hey there.

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:38.510
Hello.

00:03:38.510 --> 00:03:40.530
I've been waiting.

00:03:40.530 --> 00:03:42.490
You were off before me, weren't you?

00:03:42.840 --> 00:03:45.360
Don't look scared.

00:03:45.360 --> 00:03:48.250
We both know each other <i>really</i> well, right?

00:03:48.250 --> 00:03:50.340
Don't say that.

00:03:50.740 --> 00:03:53.940
Are you staying at someone else's house?

00:03:55.540 --> 00:03:57.160
I see.

00:03:57.160 --> 00:03:59.000
You're still running away, huh?

00:03:59.480 --> 00:04:00.960
You're quite brave.

00:04:00.960 --> 00:04:01.970
I'm going home.

00:04:03.590 --> 00:04:05.090
Hey, now.

00:04:05.090 --> 00:04:06.970
Wh-What?

00:04:07.290 --> 00:04:09.460
I'm curious about where you're living.

00:04:10.430 --> 00:04:14.770
I'd love to go there.

00:04:15.680 --> 00:04:17.550
And what will you do when you get there?

00:04:17.550 --> 00:04:19.240
Let's have a nice long talk.

00:04:19.240 --> 00:04:21.150
We were lucky enough to see each other again.

00:04:21.500 --> 00:04:25.480
No. I can't bring someone over 
without the owner's permission.

00:04:25.480 --> 00:04:29.790
Then get his permission. 
We're not doing anything wrong.

00:04:30.110 --> 00:04:33.260
I said, "no." I'm going home.

00:04:36.120 --> 00:04:38.140
Okay, how about this?

00:04:39.070 --> 00:04:45.960
If you take me home with you, I won't tell
the manager or Asami-chan about your past.

00:04:46.770 --> 00:04:49.720
And if I don't?

00:04:49.720 --> 00:04:52.020
Do I have to tell you?

00:05:00.520 --> 00:05:04.600
You're just going to come over, right?

00:05:04.600 --> 00:05:05.960
Really, really.

00:05:05.960 --> 00:05:07.700
I just want to talk!

00:05:08.080 --> 00:05:10.410
I can ask the owner, right?

00:05:10.410 --> 00:05:14.540
Of course. I'll be gone
by the time he gets home.

00:05:15.250 --> 00:05:17.040
Keep your promise, okay?

00:05:17.040 --> 00:05:20.840
Of course! It'll be fine!

00:05:25.970 --> 00:05:28.570
<b>Got it. Thanks.</b>

00:05:25.970 --> 00:05:29.930
<b>Today</b>

00:05:25.970 --> 00:05:29.930
<b>I'm bringing over someone from work. 
They'll be gone before you get home.</b>

00:05:28.070 --> 00:05:29.930
<b>Just wanted to let you know. 
Don't worry or anything.</b>

00:05:33.850 --> 00:05:36.100
It's cramped, but nice and clean.

00:05:36.520 --> 00:05:38.490
He must be the neat-freak type.

00:05:39.490 --> 00:05:41.440
I do the chores.

00:05:41.440 --> 00:05:43.190
I see.

00:05:43.710 --> 00:05:45.910
How long have you been here?

00:05:46.660 --> 00:05:48.750
About two months.

00:05:49.480 --> 00:05:52.160
He's been letting you stay here 
for two months?

00:05:52.160 --> 00:05:53.760
Yeah...

00:05:53.760 --> 00:05:55.920
What else besides chores?

00:05:55.920 --> 00:05:57.000
What else?

00:05:57.000 --> 00:05:59.960
You're not having sex with him?

00:06:01.020 --> 00:06:02.490
I-It's not like that...

00:06:02.490 --> 00:06:03.050
What?

00:06:03.050 --> 00:06:05.480
You're not? Why?

00:06:05.480 --> 00:06:07.180
"Why?"

00:06:07.180 --> 00:06:10.570
I don't understand why a man would let 
a teenage girl live with him for months

00:06:10.570 --> 00:06:12.140
and not have sex with her.

00:06:16.080 --> 00:06:19.690
Well, that means it's been a while 
for both of us.

00:06:20.040 --> 00:06:22.640
You said we'd just talk!

00:06:22.640 --> 00:06:27.530
When I'm alone with a cute girl, 
I can't control myself.

00:06:27.840 --> 00:06:28.990
That's not—

00:06:28.990 --> 00:06:31.710
We did it every day when you stayed with me!

00:06:31.710 --> 00:06:33.990
You like having sex, don't you?

00:06:33.990 --> 00:06:35.080
That's not the problem!

00:06:38.180 --> 00:06:39.790
Ow...

00:06:41.020 --> 00:06:42.290
That was mean.

00:06:42.860 --> 00:06:44.800
It wasn't even a big deal before.

00:06:45.300 --> 00:06:46.110
No...

00:06:46.110 --> 00:06:48.940
Don't worry. I'll be gentle.

00:06:53.990 --> 00:06:57.100
<i>Why did I let someone like this 
into my house?</i>

00:06:58.070 --> 00:07:02.060
<i>Because if he tells everyone, 
Asami won't be my friend anymore,</i>

00:07:02.850 --> 00:07:04.150
<i>the cops will find out...</i>

00:07:04.920 --> 00:07:08.400
<i>And it will cause problems for Yoshida-san!</i>

00:07:09.380 --> 00:07:11.460
<i>I can't let that happen.</i>

00:07:14.500 --> 00:07:15.490
...ahead.

00:07:16.630 --> 00:07:19.000
I said, "Go ahead."

00:07:19.710 --> 00:07:20.830
Sayu!

00:07:27.500 --> 00:07:30.090
Sayu, is this your boyfriend?

00:07:32.550 --> 00:07:34.010
Can I kick him out?

00:07:38.600 --> 00:07:39.930
Who the hell are you?

00:07:41.400 --> 00:07:43.240
Yaguchi Kyouya.

00:07:43.240 --> 00:07:45.370
You work at the same place as Sayu?

00:07:45.370 --> 00:07:46.940
That's right.

00:07:46.940 --> 00:07:49.820
I came over 'cause she said I could.

00:07:50.900 --> 00:07:52.030
What were you doing?

00:07:53.910 --> 00:07:55.740
Couldn't you tell?

00:07:55.740 --> 00:07:57.990
We were about to have sex.

00:07:57.990 --> 00:07:59.340
What the hell?

00:07:59.340 --> 00:08:00.830
Why are you so mad?

00:08:00.830 --> 00:08:03.960
She was staying in my apartment 
a few months ago.

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:09.680
From the look of it, 
you really haven't done anything to her.

00:08:09.680 --> 00:08:12.040
You have a teenage girl living with you, 
and you're only making her do chores?

00:08:12.040 --> 00:08:13.930
Are you pretending to be newlyweds?

00:08:13.930 --> 00:08:14.800
You little shit...

00:08:14.800 --> 00:08:18.470
She's offering to let you have sex with her 
in exchange for a place to stay.

00:08:18.470 --> 00:08:20.780
You should take her up on it.

00:08:21.230 --> 00:08:22.940
Oh, I get it.

00:08:22.940 --> 00:08:27.260
You feel good saying "no," 
like you're saving her.

00:08:27.260 --> 00:08:28.620
I...

00:08:32.210 --> 00:08:33.610
Just so you know,

00:08:33.610 --> 00:08:37.920
we're both criminals, since her parents 
haven't said she can stay with us.

00:08:37.920 --> 00:08:42.330
She says she doesn't want to go home. 
I can't force her.

00:08:45.130 --> 00:08:47.340
You really don't get it.

00:08:50.290 --> 00:08:53.340
So are you going to take care of her forever?

00:08:54.390 --> 00:08:57.210
Raise her forever?

00:08:57.210 --> 00:08:59.680
What about college? Getting a job?

00:09:00.130 --> 00:09:04.920
You can't do a thing. You're not her dad.

00:09:05.680 --> 00:09:08.610
I know that.

00:09:09.810 --> 00:09:15.240
Is it wrong to want to save her anyway?

00:09:16.290 --> 00:09:17.660
I...

00:09:18.960 --> 00:09:25.180
I don't want to be one of the adults 
teaching her things that are wrong!

00:09:28.740 --> 00:09:32.180
I pity you. I'm done here.

00:09:32.590 --> 00:09:33.760
Hey!

00:09:34.300 --> 00:09:35.320
What?

00:09:35.320 --> 00:09:38.300
Stay the hell away from Sayu!

00:09:39.910 --> 00:09:44.240
I don't think I could get it up anyway, 
if it meant dealing with a guy

00:09:44.240 --> 00:09:46.460
who'd rather jerk off 
to his own sense of self-righteousness.

00:09:46.460 --> 00:09:48.980
I promise I'll leave her alone.

00:09:49.720 --> 00:09:54.350
Also, if you kick her out after all you said, 
it'll be really pathetic.

00:09:54.350 --> 00:09:56.190
I'm not going to do that.

00:10:00.020 --> 00:10:02.160
<i>You bastards...</i>

00:10:02.880 --> 00:10:06.620
<i>None of you saved her.</i>

00:10:07.270 --> 00:10:12.250
<i>You just hurt her more 
and then threw her away.</i>

00:10:12.820 --> 00:10:16.130
<i>What's wrong with me trying to save her?</i>

00:10:16.130 --> 00:10:20.840
<i>If you don't want me to do it, 
then you should have!</i>

00:10:27.570 --> 00:10:28.780
Sayu.

00:10:29.770 --> 00:10:31.690
I made him leave.

00:10:32.310 --> 00:10:36.280
Yoshida-san, what happened to me?

00:10:38.020 --> 00:10:45.020
I slept with him before... many times. 
Like it was normal.

00:10:46.480 --> 00:10:48.910
A lot. It was a lot of times.

00:10:49.440 --> 00:10:52.000
Sayu, it's okay now.

00:10:53.350 --> 00:10:58.960
But when he was about to do it again, 
I got scared.

00:11:04.600 --> 00:11:05.770
That's okay.

00:11:05.770 --> 00:11:08.150
That's normal!

00:11:08.150 --> 00:11:10.500
But... But I...

00:11:10.870 --> 00:11:14.400
I've done it so many times. 
This shouldn't be happening now!

00:11:14.400 --> 00:11:17.640
It's okay. You've done nothing wrong.

00:11:18.630 --> 00:11:21.480
You did the right thing to turn him down. 
I'm proud.

00:11:22.340 --> 00:11:27.640
But since I turned him down, 
he'll tell everyone.

00:11:27.640 --> 00:11:33.620
The cops will come, 
and maybe you'll get in trouble.

00:11:35.280 --> 00:11:38.380
That's my fault, for letting you stay here.

00:11:38.380 --> 00:11:39.480
That's not—!

00:11:39.480 --> 00:11:40.590
Please!

00:11:41.040 --> 00:11:44.250
Just think about yourself more!

00:11:44.250 --> 00:11:47.660
Why do you try to keep hurting yourself?

00:11:47.660 --> 00:11:51.690
They all hurt you 
and didn't think anything was wrong.

00:11:52.140 --> 00:11:58.330
So if you don't care about yourself, 
there'll be nobody to protect you!

00:11:59.560 --> 00:12:04.410
Why do you try to protect me like this?

00:12:05.510 --> 00:12:07.380
I don't know.

00:12:08.200 --> 00:12:11.200
Yoshida-san, I'm sorry.

00:12:11.200 --> 00:12:12.750
Don't apologize.

00:12:13.840 --> 00:12:17.960
I want you to be a normal teenager.

00:12:18.320 --> 00:12:25.680
Going to school, making friends, 
learning things, and growing up.

00:12:25.960 --> 00:12:32.140
I know it's selfish, 
but seeing you not able to do that hurts.

00:12:33.320 --> 00:12:38.230
I don't know if I'm doing this 
for you or me anymore.

00:12:39.160 --> 00:12:44.700
But I want you to be able to care about you.

00:12:46.080 --> 00:12:48.980
Yeah... Thank you.

00:12:50.670 --> 00:12:53.180
I'll do my best.

00:13:01.880 --> 00:13:03.660
Did something happen yesterday?

00:13:04.550 --> 00:13:08.440
I'm asking if something happened with Yaguchi?

00:13:09.670 --> 00:13:11.960
Yaguchi-san? Why?

00:13:14.070 --> 00:13:16.560
Sayu-chaso, I really don't like that about you.

00:13:18.960 --> 00:13:20.690
W-Wait!

00:13:23.020 --> 00:13:24.650
What?

00:13:24.650 --> 00:13:27.080
Did you do something to Sayu-chaso yesterday?

00:13:29.050 --> 00:13:32.560
I suggested we go to her place and have sex,

00:13:32.560 --> 00:13:33.750
but she turned me down.

00:13:33.750 --> 00:13:36.320
Of course she did! Are you stupid?

00:13:36.320 --> 00:13:39.670
How was I supposed to know 
if she'd want to before I asked?

00:13:39.670 --> 00:13:41.880
You shouldn't have to ask!

00:13:41.880 --> 00:13:44.880
You didn't try to do anything 
after she said no, right?

00:13:44.880 --> 00:13:48.220
Maybe I did, a little.

00:13:51.650 --> 00:13:53.600
That hurts.

00:13:53.600 --> 00:13:58.000
It's awful to hurt somebody 
who's already hurt.

00:13:58.000 --> 00:13:59.400
And you're awful.

00:14:00.230 --> 00:14:01.520
Apologize to her.

00:14:02.190 --> 00:14:03.190
Apologize.

00:14:03.190 --> 00:14:06.140
Fine, I'll apologize. I'll apologize!

00:14:06.140 --> 00:14:07.780
Excuse me!

00:14:08.120 --> 00:14:09.800
You'd better apologize.

00:14:09.800 --> 00:14:11.460
Fine, fine.

00:14:14.020 --> 00:14:15.590
What do you need?

00:14:16.880 --> 00:14:19.590
There are goody-goodies everywhere.

00:14:20.980 --> 00:14:22.710
I'm sorry about yesterday.

00:14:23.890 --> 00:14:27.050
I don't apologize for asking.

00:14:27.050 --> 00:14:30.360
But I admit I got a little rough.

00:14:30.820 --> 00:14:34.810
Why didn't you tell Asami about us?

00:14:36.230 --> 00:14:42.730
If you told her we'd slept together before, 
she might've not been so mad.

00:14:42.730 --> 00:14:47.530
I promised not to tell 
if you brought me over, right?

00:14:50.150 --> 00:14:52.200
Why are you laughing?

00:14:52.200 --> 00:14:55.860
Well... You're pretty weird, Yaguchi-san.

00:14:57.670 --> 00:15:03.590
I'm not ready to forgive you for yesterday, 
but I don't feel mad anymore.

00:15:04.160 --> 00:15:09.560
But if you try that again, I'll get mad.

00:15:11.250 --> 00:15:12.810
Scary.

00:15:12.810 --> 00:15:16.810
And I learned you have lots 
of scary guard dogs. So I won't.

00:15:17.620 --> 00:15:22.520
It's such a waste, what that guy's doing.

00:15:22.890 --> 00:15:28.790
He's making you into such a fine woman, 
and he still won't sleep with you.

00:15:35.680 --> 00:15:39.240
<i>Yoshida-san and Asami protected me.</i>

00:15:43.650 --> 00:15:46.510
Yoshida-san's staying at work today.

00:15:46.510 --> 00:15:47.300
Seriously?

00:15:47.300 --> 00:15:54.260
<b>Sorry, there was some trouble at work, 
and I need to take care of it today. I'll probably be staying at work.</b>

00:15:47.300 --> 00:15:54.260
<b>I'm really sorry I can't be at home so soon 
after what happened yesterday.</b>

00:15:47.300 --> 00:15:54.260
<b>I'm really sorry. Try not to go out, 
and message me if anything happens.</b>

00:15:47.660 --> 00:15:51.370
"I'm really sorry. Try not to go out."

00:15:51.370 --> 00:15:54.260
Wow, he's so worried! Lol, he's like your dad!

00:15:54.260 --> 00:15:57.690
Well, I did something to make him worry.

00:15:57.690 --> 00:15:59.720
It's not your fault, Sayu-chaso.

00:16:00.900 --> 00:16:02.160
Wait!

00:16:02.160 --> 00:16:06.810
I'll tell him that I'll stay
over and protect you!

00:16:07.360 --> 00:16:09.050
Is it okay for you to stay over?

00:16:09.050 --> 00:16:10.970
It's fine!

00:16:10.970 --> 00:16:12.990
Your parents won't worry?

00:16:12.990 --> 00:16:14.680
It's fine!

00:16:14.680 --> 00:16:16.760
Nobody'll be at home tonight anyway.

00:16:16.760 --> 00:16:18.380
I see.

00:16:19.910 --> 00:16:22.410
<b>Sorry. That'd be great if you could help. Thanks.</b>

00:16:22.410 --> 00:16:23.820
You heard him.

00:16:23.820 --> 00:16:26.630
Sweet, we're together the whole night!

00:16:26.630 --> 00:16:28.200
"Sweet," huh?

00:16:29.400 --> 00:16:32.780
Come with me first.

00:16:32.780 --> 00:16:34.340
There's a place I want to go.

00:16:34.650 --> 00:16:36.030
Sure.

00:16:36.030 --> 00:16:36.940
Thanks.

00:16:36.940 --> 00:16:40.300
We'll stop by my house 
so I can get my things together.

00:16:46.000 --> 00:16:47.360
I'm back.

00:16:48.310 --> 00:16:49.820
Let's go.

00:16:51.700 --> 00:16:54.400
Asami, you've got a really big house, huh?

00:16:55.760 --> 00:16:59.920
My dad's a politician, and my mom's a lawyer.

00:16:59.920 --> 00:17:00.990
I see.

00:17:01.410 --> 00:17:04.480
So they've got more money 
than they need, and a big house?

00:17:04.480 --> 00:17:05.960
Silly, huh?

00:17:07.750 --> 00:17:08.970
Actually...

00:17:10.160 --> 00:17:13.550
I think it's a first time 
I've told a friend about my house.

00:17:13.550 --> 00:17:15.160
I see.

00:17:20.150 --> 00:17:21.480
Hey, Asami.

00:17:22.360 --> 00:17:23.480
I...

00:17:23.480 --> 00:17:25.230
I came here from Hokkaido.

00:17:26.760 --> 00:17:29.190
That's really far away.

00:17:30.080 --> 00:17:32.090
I ran away from home 
after some stuff happened.

00:17:32.640 --> 00:17:37.750
I got here by staying at different guys' places, 
including Yaguchi-san's.

00:17:38.660 --> 00:17:40.390
I see.

00:17:40.390 --> 00:17:41.140
But...

00:17:41.620 --> 00:17:45.000
When I met Yoshida-san, 
he was really nice to me.

00:17:45.000 --> 00:17:45.620
Yeah.

00:17:45.930 --> 00:17:47.770
And I met you, too.

00:17:47.770 --> 00:17:52.180
And I finally understood 
how stupid I was being.

00:17:58.910 --> 00:18:00.250
Pretty, huh?

00:18:00.250 --> 00:18:02.380
This is my favorite spot.

00:18:02.380 --> 00:18:05.060
Even in Tokyo, 
you can still see the stars like this.

00:18:05.390 --> 00:18:09.500
Kinda scary, huh? I couldn't believe it 
when I saw them the first time.

00:18:11.250 --> 00:18:14.960
My parents have always been really busy.

00:18:14.960 --> 00:18:18.330
I was left all alone in that big house.

00:18:18.330 --> 00:18:19.640
I see.

00:18:19.640 --> 00:18:23.920
I tried dressing up like a gyaru 
to get my parents' attention.

00:18:23.920 --> 00:18:27.710
My mom practically passed out, 
and my dad got super-pissed.

00:18:29.060 --> 00:18:34.710
But they didn't stop to think for a minute 
about why I was doing it.

00:18:35.380 --> 00:18:39.930
I studied hard because
I was scared of my mom.

00:18:39.930 --> 00:18:43.580
I guess she wants me to be a lawyer.

00:18:45.210 --> 00:18:46.310
You don't seem cut out for it.

00:18:47.670 --> 00:18:49.500
That's pretty mean!

00:18:49.500 --> 00:18:52.820
I'm not interested at all, though.

00:18:53.560 --> 00:18:54.900
So...

00:18:55.240 --> 00:18:56.200
So?

00:18:56.680 --> 00:18:59.200
Um... You won't laugh?

00:19:01.830 --> 00:19:04.450
I want to be an author.

00:19:05.830 --> 00:19:07.160
I see.

00:19:07.160 --> 00:19:09.660
I'll cheer you on!

00:19:09.660 --> 00:19:11.770
Really? Thanks!

00:19:11.770 --> 00:19:12.420
Of course!

00:19:13.190 --> 00:19:18.000
And so I want to study literature, 
not law, right?

00:19:18.000 --> 00:19:21.640
And when I said that, 
my mom snapped.

00:19:21.640 --> 00:19:23.390
I bet.

00:19:23.820 --> 00:19:26.590
It was the first time I really
got in an argument with my mom.

00:19:26.590 --> 00:19:31.000
And then my dad actually
took me somewhere for once.

00:19:31.000 --> 00:19:32.350
To this place.

00:19:34.770 --> 00:19:38.250
As I was staring up in shock 
at the stars, my dad said,

00:19:38.250 --> 00:19:43.380
"Your worries are nothing 
compared to these stars!"

00:19:43.910 --> 00:19:48.090
I was like, "Why are you comparing them 
to something so big, baldie?

00:19:48.090 --> 00:19:52.330
How am I supposed to compete 
with the whole universe? I'm human!"

00:19:52.700 --> 00:19:57.630
I didn't agree with a word my dad said.

00:19:57.630 --> 00:20:00.240
But when I looked up at the stars, 
I thought to myself...

00:20:00.240 --> 00:20:01.260
Thought what?

00:20:03.240 --> 00:20:09.470
Compared to the stars, 
we humans are too small to even be seen.

00:20:09.470 --> 00:20:14.410
But we all have a past of our own. A future.

00:20:14.410 --> 00:20:18.320
We're all living as best we can.

00:20:19.140 --> 00:20:23.120
You may be weirded out 
that I just started talking about myself.

00:20:23.120 --> 00:20:24.150
No...

00:20:27.730 --> 00:20:28.740
Asami?

00:20:29.500 --> 00:20:30.270
So you see...

00:20:30.840 --> 00:20:35.180
You've got a past and a future yourself.

00:20:35.640 --> 00:20:39.460
And those are yours no matter what.

00:20:39.990 --> 00:20:45.240
From listening to you, 
I can tell your past has been rough.

00:20:45.240 --> 00:20:45.930
But...

00:20:48.280 --> 00:20:50.780
There was a reason for it. I promise.

00:20:51.320 --> 00:20:52.140
It'll be okay.

00:20:58.080 --> 00:21:01.160
You got through all the bad stuff 
to make it here.

00:21:01.160 --> 00:21:02.480
You're amazing.

00:21:02.480 --> 00:21:04.380
You're such a hard worker.

00:21:04.380 --> 00:21:08.410
I can tell you told yourself 
you had to keep going.

00:21:09.690 --> 00:21:14.760
But... It's okay to take a break 
once in a while.

00:21:16.160 --> 00:21:20.500
You walked the path to get here. 
You can walk back to it.

00:21:22.550 --> 00:21:23.530
Yeah...

00:21:25.970 --> 00:21:27.560
Asami!

00:21:27.560 --> 00:21:28.650
There, there...

00:21:28.650 --> 00:21:30.200
Don't cry.

00:21:30.820 --> 00:21:32.390
Don't cry!

00:21:39.630 --> 00:21:41.680
Yoshida-san, why are you home early?

00:21:41.680 --> 00:21:45.280
I stayed all last night, so I got
out a little sooner than I expected.

00:21:45.680 --> 00:21:47.020
I see.

00:21:47.020 --> 00:21:50.330
Well...  You're always cooking for me, 
so I need to pay you back once in a while.

00:21:52.080 --> 00:21:53.470
I'm sorry.

00:21:53.470 --> 00:21:54.910
For what?

00:21:55.970 --> 00:21:58.880
Something scary happened the other day, right?

00:21:59.760 --> 00:22:02.630
I'm sorry I couldn't protect you.

00:22:03.400 --> 00:22:04.460
You protected me!

00:22:05.540 --> 00:22:07.260
But you did protect me.

00:22:11.140 --> 00:22:15.680
All this bad stuff happened to me, 
and I wanted to run away.

00:22:15.680 --> 00:22:18.480
But no matter where I went, 
the bad stuff didn't change.

00:22:19.540 --> 00:22:22.140
But I still couldn't stop myself 
from running.

00:22:22.600 --> 00:22:24.110
It hurt.

00:22:25.590 --> 00:22:26.340
But...

00:22:28.280 --> 00:22:32.870
Living with you, I finally... I finally...

00:22:34.130 --> 00:22:39.080
I-I can start to think about the future.

00:22:39.490 --> 00:22:40.680
The future?

00:22:41.830 --> 00:22:46.620
I don't have to think about where
I'm running to. But where I'm going.

00:22:47.140 --> 00:22:48.170
Sayu...

00:22:48.540 --> 00:22:49.590
So...

00:22:53.160 --> 00:22:56.390
Will you be with me just a little longer?

00:22:59.030 --> 00:23:01.100
Is that not okay?

00:23:06.650 --> 00:23:08.640
Uh, Yoshida-san?

00:23:08.640 --> 00:23:10.470
You're a good girl.

00:23:11.470 --> 00:23:15.790
I'll do everything I can to help you 
focus on the future

00:23:15.790 --> 00:23:17.420
and go back to your old life.

00:23:17.420 --> 00:23:18.750
So do your best.

00:23:19.280 --> 00:23:20.040
Yeah!

00:23:20.040 --> 00:23:21.120
Watch out!

00:23:21.730 --> 00:23:23.580
Welcome home, Yoshida-san.

00:23:24.790 --> 00:23:26.960
Thanks. I'm home.

00:23:29.970 --> 00:23:34.970
<b>Next time</b>

00:23:29.970 --> 00:23:34.970
"Yearning"

00:23:36.010 --> 00:23:39.980
<b>Watch Next Week!</b>
